{{!-- An example notice, not one to copy as it stands. Every fact only the
      owner can give is marked <mark>[to confirm: …]</mark>, visibly, and the
      audit's `placeholder-left` check reports each page that still has one,
      so a notice cannot ship half-written by accident. --}}
{{#extend "layout"}}

  {{#content "main"}}
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Example notice</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      This is the privacy notice of an example site. The marked facts are the ones a real
      owner has to supply before it is published.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Aster &amp; Oak, <mark>[to confirm: the business's legal name and postal address]</mark>.
      You can reach us about your information at <mark>[to confirm: an email address that is read]</mark>.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      This site has no forms and no accounts. With your permission, a visit counter of our
      own and Google Tag Manager use cookies to count visits and see how the site is used,
      and YouTube sets cookies when you play a video. The <a href="{{link 'cookies'}}">cookie
      page</a> lists each one, what it is for and how long it lasts. Without your permission
      none of them is set.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our host keeps a log of requests to the site, as every host does:
      <mark>[to confirm: the host's name, what its logs hold and how long it keeps them]</mark>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can withdraw your permission for cookies at any time with <em>Cookie settings</em>
      at the foot of every page. You can ask us for a copy of the information we hold about
      you, and ask us to correct or delete it. You can complain to us, and to the
      Information Commission at ico.org.uk.
      <mark>[to confirm: how to complain to the business, and whether any other right applies]</mark>
    </p>
  </div>

  {{!-- The visitor's own history of cookie choices, from this browser's log.
        `ui.history: 'privacy'` in router.js links it from the settings
        dialog. --}}
  <div class="card">
    {{consentRecord}}
  </div>
  {{/content}}

{{/extend}}
